    <string name="settings_release_notes">Release notes</string>
    <string name="notes_1_8_2">• At first launch the app asks whether you have a Bluetooth scale, and only then requests permissions\n• Setting “Do not use a scale”: no Bluetooth icon, no searching\n• The swirl step is now called Swirl</string>
    <string name="notes_1_8_1">• Recipe files (.pour) open straight in the app and land on the brewing screen\n• Presets in the 4:6 generator: save, pick and delete\n• In the 4:6 sheet “Done” stays in view and the step list no longer jumps</string>
    <string name="notes_1_8_0">• The interface in 14 languages, with a language picker in settings\n• Backup: recipes and the whole history in one file\n• Recipe steps as a timeline of badges\n• A refreshed look: rounded icons, bigger numbers, a new search field\n• Recipe order changes with a long press on the card\n• Swipe a brew away in history, with undo\n• Support for Acaia, Difluid Microbalance, Eureka Precisa and Varia AKU scales\n• Fixed the weight recorded at automatic finish</string>
    <string name="notes_1_7_2">• A brew image to share\n• Automatic finish can be switched off\n• Charts: a 50 g grid, a time axis, more height\n• Drawdown as its own step in a recipe from history\n• Fixed automatic finish when water is added after the step changes</string>
    <string name="notes_1_7_1">• A recipe from a recorded brew — straight from history\n• Hold the chart: it shows weight and time at that point\n• Delete a brew straight from the list\n• Step duration in the step list</string>
    <string name="notes_1_7_0">• AeroPress mode: the press shows up on the chart\n• Olive palette\n• The keyboard no longer covers input fields\n• Swirling no longer spoils the chart and the flow rate\n• Correct weight when finishing after the dripper is lifted</string>
    <string name="notes_1_6_1">• A bell once the last step of the recipe is over\n• Auto-finish now spots a lifted dripper on large brews too\n• A tablet in portrait no longer gets the landscape layout</string>
    <string name="notes_1_6_0">• A scale log in settings: records the exchange to a file for protocol debugging\n• The release notes dialog now holds the whole version history\n• The landscape brew layout is fixed</string>
    <string name="notes_1_5_0">• Landscape and tablet layout: sections move to a side rail, the brew screen splits into two columns\n• Lists no longer stretch across a wide screen</string>
    <string name="notes_1_4_0">• Palettes: coffee, 4:6 and standard\n• The coffee palette is calmer\n• A "What\'s new" dialog after an update</string>
    <string name="notes_1_3_0">• Tetsu Kasuya\'s 4:6 generator: dose, water, taste balance and strength in, a ready recipe out\n• Buttons on the recipe tile fit one row</string>
    <string name="notes_1_2_0">• Water rises inside the step ring\n• Swirling the dripper no longer spikes the flow rate\n• Auto-finish waits five seconds, or three once the weight goes negative</string>
    <string name="notes_1_1_0">• Experimental support for Felicita, Bookoo, Decent Scale and Timemore Black Mirror Dot\n• The app scans for every known scale at once</string>
    <string name="notes_1_0_0">First release: step-based recipes, the editor, brewing with and without scales, pace guidance, automatic finish, rescaling to the actual dose, recording a recipe from a brew, JSON import and export, history with charts, sound and vibration.</string>

    <string name="settings_scale_log_unsupported">Scale not on the supported list? Record a log and send it — that is what support for a new model is written from.</string>
    <string name="scale_log_title">Scale log</string>
    <string name="scale_log_intro">Record this when a scale will not connect or reports nonsense. The file holds what the scale sends and how the app read it. No personal data goes in.</string>
    <string name="scale_log_connected">Scale connected: %1$s</string>
    <string name="scale_log_disconnected">No scale connected. Without a connection only what the scale advertises gets recorded.</string>
    <string name="scale_log_steps">1. Switch the scale on and wait for the connection.\n2. Tap "Start recording".\n3. Wait 5 seconds with nothing on the scale.\n4. Tap "Tare" here, then the tare button on the scale itself.\n5. Put a known weight on it and wait 5 seconds.\n6. Add a little more and wait again.\n7. Take everything off.\n8. Tap "Stop".</string>
